<title>USA: U.S. weekly soybean crush 29,898,000 bushels.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekly soybean crush 29,898,000 bushels.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, meal exports in tonnes):</p>
<p>			 11/06/96    10/30/96	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 29,898,000  29,842,000    27,982,000</p>
<p> Capacity-X	34,476,000  34,476,000    33,569,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	34,668,921  34,668,921	     N/A</p>
<p> Meal Exports	 152,604     132,276	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may agree due to rounding by NOPA. R-revised.  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   11/06/96    10/30/96     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   5,108,000   5,157,000     5,185,000</p>
<p> Ind, Ky, Ohio    4,953,000   4,813,000     4,485,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  4,980,000   4,880,000     4,950,000</p>
<p> South Central    3,262,000   3,175,000     2,897,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  4,238,000   4,193,000     3,657,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 5,091,000   5,398,000     4,967,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  2,266,000   2,227,000     1,841,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	29,898,000  29,842,000    27,982,000</p>
